# GraphQL Implementation Guidelines

<rule>
name: atlas_graphql
description: Standards for implementing proper GraphQL APIs and clients
filters:
  - type: file_extension
    pattern: "\\.(?:graphql|gql|js|ts)$"
  - type: content
    pattern: "(?i)graphql|gql|query|mutation|schema|resolver"

actions:
  - type: suggest
    message: |
      When implementing GraphQL code:

      ## Schema Design
      - Use proper type definitions
      - Implement proper schema organization
      - Use proper naming conventions
      - Implement proper input types
      - Follow schema best practices

      ## Resolvers
      - Implement proper resolver functions
      - Use proper data loading patterns
      - Implement proper error handling
      - Use proper authentication/authorization
      - Follow resolver best practices

      ## Queries
      - Use proper field selection
      - Implement proper pagination
      - Use proper filtering
      - Implement proper sorting
      - Follow query best practices

      ## Mutations
      - Use proper input validation
      - Implement proper error responses
      - Use proper optimistic updates
      - Implement proper cache invalidation
      - Follow mutation best practices

      ## Client Integration
      - Use proper Apollo Client setup
      - Implement proper caching strategies
      - Use proper query hooks
      - Implement proper mutation hooks
      - Follow client best practices

examples:
  - input: "Creating a new GraphQL query"
    output: "Query uses proper field selection, pagination, and follows GraphQL best practices"

metadata:
  priority: high
  version: 1.0
</rule>